= Approved startup plan inputs

The source capsule #raw("vakint-approved-startup-plans-20261026.tar.gz") preserves
the complete, unchanged bytes of the three approved implementation plans written
at startup: #raw("VAKINT_EXTERNAL_DATA_PLAN.md"),
#raw("PRECISION_AND_INSPECTION_PLAN.md") and #raw("5L_PUSH_PLAN.md"). The original
files remain at the wrapper root. These are historical user-approved inputs,
including their recorded prompts, rather than independently maintained copies
of the current implementation documentation.

The adjacent JSON index and the internal manifest identify each file by byte
length and SHA256. The capsule contains only these three inputs, its manifest
and the small deterministic standard-library packager. Tar ownership, modes and
timestamps are normalized; gzip uses timestamp zero. Reproduction requires the
three original input files and the archived packager. The quoted development
instructions remain verbatim, including their nonsecret environment assignments.
No private environment file, license configuration, runtime ticket, cache or
generated scientific result is included.

The historical plans do not override subsequent user instructions. In particular,
current delivery focuses on the zero-momentum five-loop physical example; the
quadratic example is deferred. The full running cache is preserved separately
from the trimmed release cache. This checkpoint records inputs and does not
claim that the five-loop goal, final measurements, publication or final CI are
complete.
